Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Stitch Projection Capacity Successor Binding Revision 0.1 Threat Review

@ [threat_review_uuid] 58b3f98b-6a42-4bad-9902-4e3079594231
@ [canonical_uuid] bd6411fc-4854-4996-b1af-4e94c3abe567

& [Threats]
  + historical rewrite could make prior hashes and intent undiscoverable
  + count conflation could reduce upstream candidate diversity or admit an impossible downstream stitch set
  + malformed nine-selected fixtures could appear to test capacity while actually failing an earlier digest or correspondence check
  + silent truncation could produce a valid eight-stitch packet from an invalid nine-selected result
  + count admission could be mistaken for projected-byte admission
  + broad resume could absorb foreign main-worktree or preserved experimental changes

& [Controls]
  + additive signed successor and immutable predecessor bindings
  + separate pool selected and rendered-byte domains
  + reconstruct every upstream account identity and digest in the nine-selected adversary
  + refuse before mapping with no truncation path
  + retain independent 8192-byte validation
  + exact worktree and staged-path inventories before every commit

& [Residual]
  + implementation evidence workspace and publication gates remain open after formation and must not be claimed early
